WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.746
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:08.108
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:14.067
Unit four: Food Culture. In this unit, you will describe dishes, flavours and eating habits.

4
00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:15.957
cuisine.

5
00:00:16.657 --> 00:00:19.864
cuisine means a style of cooking from a country or region.

6
00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:22.570
Khmer cuisine uses a lot of fresh herbs.

7
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.225
Your turn. Say: cuisine.

8
00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:28.834
cuisine.

9
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.141
ingredient list.

10
00:00:31.841 --> 00:00:35.524
ingredient list means the list of all the foods used in a dish.

11
00:00:35.824 --> 00:00:38.811
Always check the ingredient list if you have an allergy.

12
00:00:39.511 --> 00:00:41.977
Your turn. Say: ingredient list.

13
00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.096
ingredient list.

14
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:47.957
spicy.

15
00:00:48.657 --> 00:00:51.957
spicy means with a hot, strong taste from chilli or pepper.

16
00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:54.024
Thai green curry is quite spicy.

17
00:00:54.724 --> 00:00:57.272
Your turn. Say: spicy.

18
00:00:59.972 --> 00:01:00.950
spicy.

19
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:02.649
bland.

20
00:01:03.349 --> 00:01:05.151
bland means without much flavour.

21
00:01:05.451 --> 00:01:07.590
Hospital food is often a bit bland.

22
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.234
Your turn. Say: bland.

23
00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:13.703
bland.

24
00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:15.706
street vendor.

25
00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:19.718
street vendor means a person who sells food or things on the street.

26
00:01:20.018 --> 00:01:22.900
The street vendor near my school sells delicious noodles.

27
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.857
Your turn. Say: street vendor.

28
00:01:28.557 --> 00:01:29.616
street vendor.

29
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:31.745
signature dish.

30
00:01:32.445 --> 00:01:36.152
signature dish means the most famous dish of a restaurant or chef.

31
00:01:36.452 --> 00:01:39.241
Fish amok is the signature dish of this restaurant.

32
00:01:39.941 --> 00:01:42.767
Your turn. Say: signature dish.

33
00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:46.828
signature dish.

34
00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:49.038
portion size.

35
00:01:49.738 --> 00:01:52.829
portion size means the amount of food served to one person.

36
00:01:53.129 --> 00:01:55.767
Portion sizes in some countries are very big.

37
00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:59.120
Your turn. Say: portion size.

38
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.053
portion size.

39
00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.167
table manners.

40
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:08.703
table manners means polite ways of behaving while eating.

41
00:02:09.003 --> 00:02:11.710
Good table manners are important at a business dinner.

42
00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.260
Your turn. Say: table manners.

43
00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.240
table manners.

44
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.366
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:22.666 --> 00:02:24.990
Nita, what's your favourite Cambodian dish?

46
00:02:26.283 --> 00:02:29.667
Fish amok! It's the signature dish of my mum's restaurant.

47
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:32.193
Is it spicy?

48
00:02:33.483 --> 00:02:38.179
Not very. It has a little chilli, but lots of coconut and herbs.

49
00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:42.063
I find some food here a bit too spicy for me.

50
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.210
Then try kuy teav. It isn't bland, but it's very mild.

51
00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:50.876
Grammar focus: Quantifiers.

52
00:02:51.176 --> 00:02:54.685
Use much and a little with uncountable nouns like sugar and rice.

53
00:02:54.985 --> 00:02:58.401
Use many and a few with countable nouns like chillies and dishes.

54
00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:02.291
For example: There isn't much sugar, and we only need a few chillies.

55
00:03:02.591 --> 00:03:06.611
Use much and many mainly in questions and negatives; a lot of works everywhere.

56
00:03:07.617 --> 00:03:10.176
Now read and listen. Eating Like a Local.

57
00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:14.403
Travellers often say that food is the best way to understand a culture.

58
00:03:15.717 --> 00:03:19.202
In Cambodia, a lot of people eat breakfast from a street vendor.

59
00:03:20.517 --> 00:03:24.780
Meals usually include rice, a soup and a few shared dishes.

60
00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:29.708
Good table manners mean waiting for the oldest person to start eating.

61
00:03:31.017 --> 00:03:35.478
Most visitors are surprised that Khmer cuisine is fresh, not just spicy.

62
00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:39.134
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.445
Food without much flavour is blank.

64
00:03:41.745 --> 00:03:45.364
A, spicy. B, bland. C, signature.

65
00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.943
The answer is B: bland.

66
00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.939
How blank rice do we need?

67
00:03:54.239 --> 00:03:56.766
A, many. B, much. C, few.

68
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.633
The answer is B: much.

69
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.917
There are only blank seats left.

70
00:04:06.217 --> 00:04:09.081
A, a little. B, a few. C, much.

71
00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:15.060
The answer is B: a few.

72
00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.724
Polite ways of behaving while eating are blank.

73
00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:23.734
A, table manners. B, portion sizes. C, ingredient lists.

74
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.075
The answer is A: table manners.

75
00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:34.372
According to the text, who starts eating first?

76
00:04:34.672 --> 00:04:38.767
A, the youngest person. B, the oldest person. C, the guest.

77
00:04:42.783 --> 00:04:44.864
The answer is B: the oldest person.

78
00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:50.477
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe a dish from your country to a foreign friend.

79
00:04:55.777 --> 00:05:02.075
Lok lak is beef with a peppery sauce. It's not very spicy, and we eat it with rice and fresh vegetables.

80
00:05:02.375 --> 00:05:04.014
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:05.017 --> 00:05:08.435
Great work today! You learned eight new words and quantifiers.

82
00:05:08.735 --> 00:05:12.595
Today's value is respect for culture. Be proud of our Khmer culture.

83
00:05:12.895 --> 00:05:15.176
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

84
00:05:15.476 --> 00:05:18.175
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

